CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "274893c2-7895-4fb2-8644-16e05d91c71c",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T18:51:25Z",
  "ticket_id": "4e55-a6ba",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "Config keys merge.strategy (direct|pr, default direct) and enforcement.strategy (local|ci|both, default local) introduced; merge-to-main.sh becomes a thin dispatcher that execs merge-to-main-direct.sh (extracted current behavior) or merge-to-main-pr.sh (new); PreToolUse hooks and .pre-commit-config.yaml entries read enforcement.strategy and short-circuit to no-op (with structured HOOK_GATE: skipped reason=enforcement.strategy=ci log) when value is ci.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system capabilities (config keys, dispatcher behavior, hook gating logic) that persist after implementation rather than one-time migration tasks"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "COMMIT-WORKFLOW.md restructured: a Step 0.6 Load enforcement profile reads enforcement.strategy and conditionally loads commit-workflow-validation.md (extracted local-validation steps including format, lint, type-check, the test-status recording call, and the review gate) when value is local or both; skips the load when ci.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time restructuring task of documentation and workflow configuration that has been completed"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Running merge-to-main.sh with merge.strategy=pr against the live digital-service-orchestra repo creates a PR via gh pr create, queues gh pr merge --auto, polls CI plus threads, programmatically resolves threads via the GraphQL resolveReviewThread mutation after addressing each in code or via REST reply, and exits zero after the merge commit lands on origin/main \u2014 verified in-session via gh run list and git log origin/main.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (the script reliably performs automated PR merging with thread resolution) phrased as ongoing behavior, though the verification clause adds minor transitional flavor"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Required-checks blocking is verified in-session on a real PR: a deliberate test PR with gh pr merge --auto queued; in-session checks confirm the PR remains in BLOCKED mergeStateStatus until each required check (CI tests, LLM review, validate-ci, platform-matrix legs, pipefail-strict, conversation-resolution) reports a green conclusion; gh pr merge --squash rejects with not mergeable until all checks pass; the PR auto-merges only after the final check turns green.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior where required checks persistently block merges until satisfied, verified through observable PR state and merge behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A dedicated story carries the COMMIT-WORKFLOW.md restructure; the story description embeds two audit criteria \u2014 (a) no enforcement bypass: every former gate's enforcement is preserved by either the conditional load OR the hook-gating, with no path that lets unreviewed/untested code reach a commit when enforcement.strategy=local; (b) no unnecessary friction: the ci path is leaner than the local path, the local path adds no new steps over the pre-epic baseline, the conditional load adds no more than 1 net Bash call. The story closes only when the standard review/remediation cycle reports zero important findings against these criteria; orchestrators are prohibited from closing the story while any important finding remains open.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time restructuring task with completion criteria (audit review cycle completion and zero important findings) that marks task closure, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "provision-ruleset.sh extended with config knobs matching the manual rules on this repo: bypass_actor_policy (always|pull_request_only), require_conversation_resolution, request_copilot_review, dismiss_stale_approvals_on_push, required_approvals; CodeQL and code-quality rules are deferred to a follow-on placeholder epic.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes completed extension work with specific configuration additions and deferred items, phrased as a one-time implementation task"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "/dso:onboarding asks the user to choose between direct and pr (defaulting to direct for non-technical users) and writes the choice to dso-config.conf; selecting pr triggers provision-ruleset.sh automatically.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior where the onboarding flow supports user choice persistence and conditional automation, outcomes that remain true after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "ci-generator.sh and ci-skeleton-templates.md gain a sibling PR-mode template variant exposed via ci-generator.sh --mode=pr-protected; the generated workflow includes the Resolve-and-fetch DSO plugin assets step from the CI parity epic.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (ci-generator.sh supporting a pr-protected mode with specific workflow steps) that will remain true after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "create-dso-app.sh writes merge.strategy=direct and enforcement.strategy=local to the new project's dso-config.conf and does NOT provision a Ruleset; the digital-service-orchestra-nextjs-template repo's checked-in dso-config.conf matches.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable configuration state that persists in the system after the work, where specific values are written to config files and match across repos"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "This project's dso-config.conf is updated within this epic to set merge.strategy=pr and enforcement.strategy=local; a directional note is added to the operational-flip epic that enforcement.strategy flips to ci when that epic runs.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes specific configuration changes and a directional note being added as one-time updates, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "plugins/dso/scripts/onboarding/github-bootstrap.sh updated so its git push origin HEAD:main escape hatch is conditional on merge.strategy=direct OR an as-yet-unprovisioned ruleset; on PR-mode projects with a pre-existing ruleset, the script either uses the admin bypass when configured or surfaces a clear error directing the user to disable the ruleset for the bootstrap window.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable script behavior that conditionally handles git push operations based on merge strategy and ruleset configuration, persisting after this work"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "merge-to-main-direct.sh and merge-to-main-pr.sh both emit CONFLICT_DATA output with the same schema on conflict, OR merge-to-main-pr.sh documents that conflicts are surfaced via a different signal \u2014 plugins/dso/skills/resolve-conflicts/SKILL.md is updated to handle whichever shape is chosen; verified by a regression test.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior where two merge scripts emit consistent conflict output and documentation reflects the chosen schema, verifiable by ongoing regression tests"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Happy-path E2E: a real merge-to-main.sh --strategy=pr run on this repo's worktree completes autonomously \u2014 PR created, CI passes, threads resolved, branch merged, script exits 0; verified in-session via git log origin/main showing the merge commit.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time verification task (running the script and observing successful merge) rather than an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Direct-mode regression: on a project with merge.strategy=direct and no GitHub remote, merge-to-main.sh behaves identically to the pre-epic baseline \u2014 no new prompts, no new errors, same exit code.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable behavioral property of the system (merge script compatibility under specific conditions) that should remain true after work completes"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Thread-resolution path: a deliberately seeded blocking review thread on a test PR is resolved by the autonomous loop within the wait window, OR (negative test) a thread the agent cannot programmatically resolve causes the loop to escalate to the user with the PR URL rather than spinning indefinitely.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system capabilities for handling review threads and escalation that persist after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    }
  ]
}
